  "2026-08-27T17:34:25.151Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence: the real Unix-domain socket rejection test now uses a deliberately short /tmp fixture root, preserving the non-regular-file security assertion while remaining below macOS Node 24 socket-path limits. The focused linked test passed, the full 585-file suite passed, and exact repository coverage remains 100/100/100/100. Hosted macOS validation remains part of the PR matrix."
  "2026-08-27T21:30:45.590Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance evidence 2026-08-27: explicit workflow_dispatch run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/33117244185 completed successfully on head 9bcb5817bee7120896bb0a720f1a44e117e1e8f5. Passing jobs: Ubuntu Node 22 (98674934349), Ubuntu Node 24 (98674934126), Ubuntu Node 25 (98674934212), macOS Node 24 (98674934248), and Windows Node 24 (98674934229). This satisfies the full Nightly Validation matrix before renewed close/release."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T17:34:25.641Z","harness:codex",Cross-platform Unix socket tests should minimize the pathname at fixture construction; truncating semantics or mocking socket identity would hide the security behavior being tested.
  "2026-08-27T21:30:46.094Z","harness:codex",Portable special-file security tests need both semantic negative-control proof and explicit hosted platform evidence; a passing local Linux run or one macOS job does not satisfy a declared Linux/macOS/Windows matrix.
